note Omega Node durable journal and restart recovery (DRA-289). Concatenate
note after transport.om, pool.om, super.om, sched.om and
note seed/authority/action.om, before auth.om, which journals through it.
note While no journal is open every append succeeds without writing, so the
note authority layer also runs memory-only.
note File DIR/journal: a 64-byte header, then 128-byte records. Header words:
note 0 magic, 1 format version 2, 2 record size 128, 3..6 objective identity,
note 7 FNV-1a 64 of words 0..6. Record words: 0 type, 1 seq (1, 2, 3, ...
note with no gap), 2 fence, 3..14 payload, 15 FNV-1a 64 of words 0..14.
note Types and payloads:
note 1 OPEN     3 pid, 4 authority generation of the new creator, 5 the
note                scheduler policy version SPVER it was written under
note 2 ADMIT    3 job id, 4 dependency topics, 5 flags, 6 resource request,
note                7 table slot
note 3 START    3..6 operation identity, 7 class, 8 job id, 9 attempt, 10 gen
note 4 DONE     3..6 operation identity, 7 outcome (0 UNKNOWN, 1 not
note                performed, 2 performed), 8 job id, 9 how (1 reported,
note                2 worker lost, 3 in flight at restart, 4 key present,
note                5 key absent, 6 no external effect)
note 5 RELEASE  3 job id, 4 outcome (the job's outcome; 300 cancelled)
note 6 REVOKE   3 new generation
note 7 PAUSE    3 1 paused, 0 resumed
note 8 CANCEL   3 job id
note 10         reserved (RESULT, DRA-292)
note 11 POLICY  3 policy, 4 window, 5 dispatch budget, 6 bypass budget,
note                7 ticket lifetime, 8 capacities (packed like a request):
note                the whole setting; the last one wins
note 12 GOAL    3 job id, 4 topics, 5 estimate ms, 6 uncertainty ms
note 13 FAIR    3 dispatch event, 4 assigned slot bitmap, 5 bypassed slot
note                bitmap, 6 cursor, 7 reserved slot + 1, 8 slots a
note                publication made ready (sched.om's ring)
note A header of another version (1 included) is refused (21); an OPEN
note written under another SPVER is refused at replay (33).
note Order: a transition is appended and fdatasync'd before anything acts on
note it or publishes it. An append whose write or sync fails marks the journal
note failed and every later append is refused, so nothing is acted on that
note might not be durable.
note Fencing: DIR/lock is held with flock(LOCK_EX) for the creator's life. It
note is opened close-on-exec, so tools never hold it, but forked workers do:
note a new creator cannot open the journal until every worker of the old one
note has exited. Each open appends OPEN with the next fence number, and every
note record carries the fence of the creator that wrote it.
note Torn tail: a partial last record, or a last full record whose checksum or
note seq is wrong, was never acknowledged and is cut off. A bad record that is
note not the last is corruption: the open is refused and nothing is changed.
note Compatibility: a header whose magic, version, record size or checksum
note differs is refused (21), never reinterpreted; an objective identity that
note differs is refused (22).
text jnjour "/journal"
text jnlock "/lock"
text jnkey "/k."
global jon ulong 1
global jbad ulong 1
global jfd int 1
global jlk int 1
global jseq ulong 1
global jsz ulong 1
global jfence ulong 1
global jgen ulong 1
global jcrash ulong 1
global jdir uchar 128
global jdn ulong 1
global jpath uchar 160
global jact ulong 1024
global jjob ulong 2048
global jstat ulong 8
note Policy replay tables (DRA-398), per job entry k: jreq request, jslot
note slot at admission, jbyp bypass count, jrdy 1 once a publication made
note it ready; jsl slot -> job entry + 1 while admitted and not released;
note jpol 0 seen, 1..5 policy words, 6 caps; jgoal per k: 0 seen, 1
note topics, 2 estimate, 3 uncertainty; jfair 0 last event, 1 cursor, 2
note reserved job entry + 1, 3 seen.
global jreq ulong 256
global jslot ulong 256
global jbyp ulong 256
global jrdy ulong 256
global jsl ulong 64
global jpol ulong 8
global jgoal ulong 1024
global jfair ulong 4

note Fault injection for the recovery tests: exit 77 at point p when armed.
fn jn_hit p ulong to void
if and gt p 0 eq get jcrash 0 p
exit 77
end
end

fn jn_sum r view ulong 16 n ulong to ulong
h = ulong 14695981039346656037
for i ulong n bound 16
v = get r i
for b ulong 8
h = mul xor h and shr v mul b 8 255 1099511628211
end
end
ret h
end

fn jn_enc r view ulong 16 b edit uchar 128 to void
for i ulong 16
v = get r i
for k ulong 8
put b add mul i 8 k uchar and shr v mul k 8 255
end
end
end

fn jn_dec b view uchar 128 r edit ulong 16 to void
for i ulong 16
v = ulong 0
for k ulong 8
v = or v shl ulong get b add mul i 8 k mul k 8
end
put r i v
end
end

note DIR plus name k (0 journal, 1 lock, 2 key prefix) in jpath; the length.
fn jn_name k ulong to ulong
n = get jdn 0
for i ulong n bound 128
put jpath i get jdir i
end
m = len jnjour
if eq k 1
m = len jnlock
end
if eq k 2
m = len jnkey
end
for i ulong m bound 16
b = get jnkey 0
if eq k 0
b = get jnjour i
end
if eq k 1
b = get jnlock i
end
if eq k 2
b = get jnkey i
end
put jpath add n i b
end
ret add n m
end

note The key path DIR/k.<v> of an idempotent effect; the length.
fn jn_keyp v ulong to ulong
n = jn_name 2
d = new uchar 20 0
x = v
k = ulong 20
for i ulong 20
k = sub k 1
put d k uchar add rem x 10 48
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
for i ulong sub 20 k bound 20
put jpath add n i get d add k i
end
ret add n sub 20 k
end

fn jn_reset to void
for i ulong 1024
put jact i 0
end
for i ulong 2048
put jjob i 0
end
for i ulong 8
put jstat i 0
put jpol i 0
end
for i ulong 256
put jreq i 0
put jslot i 0
put jbyp i 0
put jrdy i 0
end
for i ulong 1024
put jgoal i 0
end
for i ulong 64
put jsl i 0
end
for i ulong 4
put jfair i 0
end
put jon 0 0
put jbad 0 0
put jseq 0 0
put jsz 0 0
put jfence 0 0
put jgen 0 0
end

note Action table, 64 entries of 16 words: 0 used, 1..4 operation identity,
note 5 class, 6 state (as action.om: 1 ready, 2 in flight, 3 UNKNOWN,
note 4 performed), 7 attempt, 8 gen, 9 job id. -1 when absent.
fn jn_afind r view ulong 16 to long
for k ulong 64
b = mul k 16
if ne get jact b 0
m = true
for i ulong 4
if ne get jact add b add 1 i get r add 3 i
m = false
end
end
if m
ret long k
end
end
end
ret neg long 1
end

note Job table, 256 entries of 8 words: 0 used, 1 job id, 2 deps, 3 flags,
note 4 released, 5 outcome, 6 cancelled, 7 action entry + 1 of its last START.
fn jn_jfind id ulong to long
for k ulong 256
if and ne get jjob mul k 8 0 eq get jjob add mul k 8 1 id
ret long k
end
end
ret neg long 1
end

fn jn_jnew id ulong to long
for k ulong 256
b = mul k 8
if eq get jjob b 0
for i ulong 8
put jjob add b i 0
end
put jjob b 1
put jjob add b 1 id
ret long k
end
end
ret neg long 1
end

fn jn_maxg g ulong to void
if gt g get jgen 0
put jgen 0 g
end
end

fn jn_astart r view ulong 16 to ulong
k = jn_afind r
if lt k 0
for i ulong 64
if eq get jact mul i 16 0
k = long i
break
end
end
end
if lt k 0
ret 25
end
b = mul ulong k 16
if ne get jact b 0
if ne get jact add b 6 1
ret 25
end
end
put jact b 1
for i ulong 4
put jact add b add 1 i get r add 3 i
end
put jact add b 5 get r 7
put jact add b 6 2
put jact add b 7 get r 9
put jact add b 8 get r 10
put jact add b 9 get r 8
jn_maxg get r 10
j = jn_jfind get r 8
if ge j 0
put jjob add mul ulong j 8 7 add ulong k 1
end
ret 0
end

fn jn_adone r view ulong 16 to ulong
k = jn_afind r
if lt k 0
ret 25
end
b = mul ulong k 16
s = get jact add b 6
if not or eq s 2 eq s 3
ret 25
end
o = get r 7
if gt o 2
ret 25
end
v = ulong 3
if eq o 1
v = 1
end
if eq o 2
v = 4
end
put jact add b 6 v
ret 0
end

note Apply one durable record to the recovery tables; 0, 24 unknown type,
note 25 a transition the tables refuse (START of a performed operation, a
note DONE without a START, a second ADMIT or RELEASE, a policy record that
note does not hold), 33 an OPEN of another scheduler policy version.
fn jn_apply r view ulong 16 to ulong
t = get r 0
if eq t 1
if ne get r 5 SPVER
ret 33
end
put jfence 0 get r 2
jn_maxg get r 4
ret 0
end
if eq t 2
ret jn_aadmit r
end
if eq t 3
ret jn_astart r
end
if eq t 4
ret jn_adone r
end
if or eq t 5 eq t 8
j = jn_jfind get r 3
if lt j 0
ret 25
end
b = mul ulong j 8
if eq t 8
put jjob add b 6 1
if eq get jfair 2 add ulong j 1
put jfair 2 0
end
ret 0
end
if ne get jjob add b 4 0
ret 25
end
put jjob add b 4 1
put jjob add b 5 get r 4
s = get jslot ulong j
if eq get jsl s add ulong j 1
put jsl s 0
end
ret 0
end
if eq t 6
jn_maxg get r 3
ret 0
end
if eq t 7
put jstat 2 get r 3
ret 0
end
if gt t 10
ret jn_apol r
end
ret 24
end

note ADMIT into the tables: a new job entry with its request and slot; a
note slot another unreleased job holds is refused (25).
fn jn_aadmit r view ulong 16 to ulong
if ge jn_jfind get r 3 0
ret 25
end
s = get r 7
if ge s 64
ret 25
end
if ne get jsl s 0
ret 25
end
j = jn_jnew get r 3
if lt j 0
ret 25
end
k = ulong j
put jjob add mul k 8 2 get r 4
put jjob add mul k 8 3 get r 5
put jreq k get r 6
put jslot k s
put jbyp k 0
put jrdy k 0
put jsl s add k 1
ret 0
end

note POLICY, GOAL and FAIR into the tables (types 11..13); 24 any other.
fn jn_apol r view ulong 16 to ulong
t = get r 0
if eq t 11
if not sched_polok get r 3 get r 4 get r 5 get r 6 get r 7
ret 25
end
put jpol 0 1
for i ulong 6
put jpol add i 1 get r add i 3
end
ret 0
end
if eq t 12
j = jn_jfind get r 3
if lt j 0
ret 25
end
b = mul ulong j 4
put jgoal b 1
for i ulong 3
put jgoal add b add i 1 get r add i 4
end
ret 0
end
if eq t 13
ret jn_afair r
end
ret 24
end

note FAIR into the tables. A decision record (word 8 zero) must follow the
note last event; a readiness record (word 8 the slots a publication made
note ready, nothing assigned or bypassed) may share it, since publication
note does not count as a dispatch event. The cursor must lie in the
note table; assigned and bypassed slots must be disjoint and hold live
note ready jobs (no deps, or made ready by an earlier readiness record);
note slots made ready must hold live waiting jobs; the reserved slot a live
note ready job this record did not assign. Live: admitted, not released,
note not cancelled. Nothing changes otherwise (25). Assigned jobs' bypass
note counts restart at 0, bypassed ones go up by one, jobs made ready are
note marked ready.
fn jn_afair r view ulong 16 to ulong
am = get r 4
bm = get r 5
rd = get r 8
if not jn_fevt get r 3 or am bm rd
ret 25
end
if or ge get r 6 64 ne and am bm 0
ret 25
end
if or not jn_fok or am bm 1 not jn_fok rd 2
ret 25
end
rs = get r 7
if gt rs 64
ret 25
end
rk = ulong 0
if gt rs 0
if ne and shr am sub rs 1 1 0
ret 25
end
if not jn_fok shl ulong 1 sub rs 1 1
ret 25
end
rk = get jsl sub rs 1
end
for s ulong 64
if ne and shr am s 1 0
put jbyp sub get jsl s 1 0
end
if ne and shr bm s 1 0
k = sub get jsl s 1
put jbyp k add get jbyp k 1
end
if ne and shr rd s 1 0
put jrdy sub get jsl s 1 1
end
end
put jfair 0 get r 3
put jfair 1 get r 6
put jfair 2 rk
put jfair 3 1
ret 0
end

note Event order of a FAIR at event ev with assigned or bypassed slots ab
note and slots made ready rd: a readiness record (ab empty) is never also a
note decision, even as the first FAIR; decisions come strictly after the
note last event, readiness at or after it.
fn jn_fevt ev ulong ab ulong rd ulong to bool
if and ne rd 0 ne ab 0
ret false
end
if eq get jfair 3 0
ret true
end
if ne rd 0
ret ge ev get jfair 0
end
ret gt ev get jfair 0
end

note Does every slot set in bitmap m hold a live job that is ready (kind 1:
note no deps, or made ready) or waiting (kind 2: deps, not made ready)?
fn jn_fok m ulong kind ulong to bool
for s ulong 64
if ne and shr m s 1 0
x = get jsl s
if eq x 0
ret false
end
k = sub x 1
b = mul k 8
if or ne get jjob add b 4 0 ne get jjob add b 6 0
ret false
end
w = and ne get jjob add b 2 0 eq get jrdy k 0
if and w eq kind 1
ret false
end
if and not w eq kind 2
ret false
end
end
end
ret true
end

fn jn_le64 b view uchar 128 off ulong to ulong
v = ulong 0
for k ulong 8
v = or v shl ulong get b add off k mul k 8
end
ret v
end

note Make DIR's entry for a new journal durable.
fn jn_dsync to ulong
fd = fopen jdir 0 get jdn 0 540672 0
if lt fd 0
ret 27
end
r = fsync int fd
x = fclose int fd
if ne r 0
ret 27
end
ret 0
end

note Create the header of an empty journal, or check an existing one.
fn jn_head fd int obj view ulong 4 to ulong
st = new uchar 128 0
h = new ulong 16 0
b = new uchar 128 0
if ne fstat fd st 0 128 0
ret 27
end
size = jn_le64 st 48
if lt size 64
if ne ftrunc fd 0 0
ret 27
end
put h 0 5786624599
put h 1 2
put h 2 128
for i ulong 4
put h add 3 i get obj i
end
put h 7 jn_sum h 7
jn_enc h b
if ne pwrite fd b 0 64 0 64
ret 27
end
if ne fsync fd 0
ret 27
end
put jsz 0 64
ret jn_dsync
end
if ne pread fd b 0 64 0 64
ret 27
end
jn_dec b h
s = jn_sum h 7
if or ne get h 0 5786624599 ne get h 7 s
ret 21
end
if or ne get h 1 2 ne get h 2 128
ret 21
end
for i ulong 4
if ne get h add 3 i get obj i
ret 22
end
end
put jsz 0 size
ret 0
end

fn jn_cut fd int off ulong to ulong
if ne ftrunc fd long off 0
ret 27
end
if ne fdsync fd 0
ret 27
end
put jstat 0 add get jstat 0 sub get jsz 0 off
put jsz 0 off
ret 0
end

note Record i into r: 0 well formed (checksum and seq), 1 not, 27 I/O.
fn jn_rd fd int i ulong r edit ulong 16 to ulong
b = new uchar 128 0
off = long add 64 mul i 128
if ne pread fd b 0 128 off 128
ret 27
end
jn_dec b r
s = jn_sum r 15
if ne get r 15 s
ret 1
end
if ne get r 1 add i 1
ret 1
end
ret 0
end

note Read every record into the tables; cut a torn tail; refuse corruption.
fn jn_scan fd int to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
n = div sub get jsz 0 64 128
rm = rem sub get jsz 0 64 128
for i ulong n bound 10000000
g = jn_rd fd i r
if eq g 27
ret 27
end
if eq g 1
if and eq add i 1 n eq rm 0
ret jn_cut fd add 64 mul i 128
end
ret 23
end
e = jn_apply r
if ne e 0
ret e
end
put jseq 0 add i 1
put jstat 1 add i 1
end
if gt rm 0
ret jn_cut fd add 64 mul n 128
end
ret 0
end

note Append record r (caller sets word 0 and the payload) and make it
note durable, after the dispatch decisions waiting in sched.om's replay
note ring (jn_drain), so no transition is durable before the scheduling
note that came before it. The tables check and take the transition first
note (jn_apply changes nothing when it refuses), so a refused transition is
note never written. 0, a table refusal, 28 write, 29 sync, 30 failed
note earlier. After 28 or 29 the journal is failed: the transition may or
note may not be durable, so the caller must not act on it, and nothing more
note is written. Without an open journal: 0.
fn jn_append r edit ulong 16 to ulong
e = jn_drain
if ne e 0
ret e
end
ret jn_put r
end

note Write the replay ring as FAIR records and empty it; then, when the
note cursor or the reservation moved without a record (a window scan that
note assigned nothing), one FAIR with empty bitmaps. 0 or as jn_put; on
note failure the ring keeps its records and dispatch stops when it fills.
note The ring is attached by jn_recover, once the scheduler holds the
note journaled state; before that, or without an open journal, it is
note emptied and nothing is written.
fn jn_drain to ulong
if or eq get jon 0 0 not sched_jattached
sched_frclear
ret 0
end
r = new ulong 16 0
n = sched_frn
for k ulong n bound 64
for i ulong 16
put r i 0
end
put r 0 13
for i ulong 6
put r add 3 i sched_frw k i
end
e = jn_put r
if ne e 0
ret e
end
end
sched_frclear
rk = ulong 0
rs = sched_stat 29
if gt rs 0
rk = get jsl sub rs 1
end
if and eq sched_stat 28 get jfair 1 eq rk get jfair 2
ret 0
end
if eq sched_stat 2 get jfair 0
ret 0
end
for i ulong 16
put r i 0
end
put r 0 13
put r 3 sched_stat 2
put r 6 sched_stat 28
put r 7 rs
ret jn_put r
end

note jn_append without the drain.
fn jn_put r edit ulong 16 to ulong
if eq get jon 0 0
ret 0
end
if ne get jbad 0 0
ret 30
end
b = new uchar 128 0
fd = get jfd 0
put r 1 add get jseq 0 1
put r 2 get jfence 0
put r 15 jn_sum r 15
e = jn_apply r
if ne e 0
ret e
end
jn_enc r b
off = long add 64 mul get jseq 0 128
if and eq get jcrash 0 6 eq get r 0 4
x = pwrite fd b 0 60 off
exit 77
end
if ne pwrite fd b 0 128 off 128
put jbad 0 1
ret 28
end
if ne fdsync fd 0
put jbad 0 1
ret 29
end
put jseq 0 add get jseq 0 1
put jsz 0 add get jsz 0 128
ret 0
end

fn jn_rec t ulong a ulong b ulong c ulong to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 t
put r 3 a
put r 4 b
put r 5 c
ret jn_append r
end

note Open (or create) the journal in directory dir (dn bytes) for objective
note obj, waiting up to ms for the lock. 0, 20 fenced (another creator or
note its workers hold the lock), 21 incompatible, 22 other objective, 23
note corrupt, 24/25 refused record, 26 path too long, 27 I/O error.
fn jn_open dir view uchar 128 dn ulong obj view ulong 4 ms ulong to ulong
if or eq dn 0 gt dn 100
ret 26
end
jn_reset
for i ulong dn bound 128
put jdir i get dir i
end
put jdn 0 dn
r = makedir jdir 0 dn 448
if and lt r 0 ne r neg long 17
ret 27
end
n = jn_name 1
lk = fopen jpath 0 n 524354 384
if lt lk 0
ret 27
end
got = false
for t ulong add ms 1 bound 100000
f = flock int lk 6
if eq f 0
got = true
break
end
if ne f neg long 11
break
end
x = sleepns 1000000
end
if not got
x = fclose int lk
ret 20
end
put jlk 0 int lk
e = jn_load obj
if ne e 0
x = fclose int lk
ret e
end
ret 0
end

fn jn_load obj view ulong 4 to ulong
n = jn_name 0
fd = fopen jpath 0 n 524354 384
if lt fd 0
ret 27
end
e = jn_head int fd obj
if eq e 0
e = jn_scan int fd
end
if ne e 0
x = fclose int fd
ret e
end
put jfd 0 int fd
put jon 0 1
put jfence 0 add get jfence 0 1
put jgen 0 add get jgen 0 1
ret jn_rec 1 ulong getpid get jgen 0 SPVER
end

note Close the journal (after draining the replay ring) and release the
note lock (other holders: forked workers).
fn jn_close to void
if ne get jon 0 0
dr = jn_drain
x = fclose get jfd 0
x = fclose get jlk 0
end
put jon 0 0
sched_jattach false
end

note Probe the key of an idempotent operation: 1 present, 0 absent, 2 error.
fn jn_probe v ulong to ulong
st = new uchar 128 0
n = jn_keyp v
r = stat jpath 0 n st 0 128
if eq r 0
ret 1
end
if eq r neg long 2
ret 0
end
ret 2
end

note Close every START left in flight by a crash with a DONE. Class 3 (an
note idempotent effect whose key DIR/k.<op word 0> is created atomically by
note the effect) is decided by its key; class 2 (no external effect) was not
note performed; anything else is UNKNOWN and is never run again.
fn jn_settle to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
for k ulong 64
b = mul k 16
if and ne get jact b 0 eq get jact add b 6 2
for i ulong 4
put r add 3 i get jact add b add 1 i
end
put r 0 4
put r 8 get jact add b 9
cl = get jact add b 5
put r 7 0
put r 9 3
if eq cl 2
put r 7 1
put r 9 6
end
if eq cl 3
p = jn_probe get r 3
if eq p 2
ret 27
end
put r 7 add 1 p
put r 9 sub 5 p
end
e = jn_append r
if ne e 0
ret e
end
put jstat 3 add get jstat 3 1
end
end
ret 0
end

note Recovery: the incarnation (the fence), then the last journaled policy
note and capacities. False when the scheduler refused one; a fence past the
note incarnation range (2^24 - 1) is refused, never folded onto an earlier
note incarnation.
fn jn_rpol to bool
if ne sched_incarnate get jfence 0 0
ret false
end
if eq get jpol 0 0
ret true
end
if ne sched_cap get jpol 6 0
ret false
end
p = get jpol 1
w = get jpol 2
d = get jpol 3
y = get jpol 4
ret eq sched_policy p w d y get jpol 5 0
end

note Creator, after jn_open and sched_new: settle in-flight operations,
note set the scheduler's incarnation to the fence (proposals made for an
note earlier creator are stale), restore the last journaled policy and
note capacities, then for each admitted job not yet released: a performed
note or UNKNOWN last operation releases it with that outcome (it never runs
note again); a cancelled job is released as cancelled; any other is
note admitted again, in admission order, into its recorded slot, with its
note bypass count and declared goal. Last, the cursor, the dispatch event
note count and the reservation (on the job's slot) from the last FAIR.
note 0 or an error (31 a restore the scheduler refused).
fn jn_recover c long to ulong
e = jn_settle
if ne e 0
ret e
end
if not jn_rpol
ret 31
end
rs = ulong 0
for k ulong 256
b = mul k 8
if and ne get jjob b 0 eq get jjob add b 4 0
o = jn_rout k
if eq o 999
x = jn_readmit k
if lt x 0
ret 31
end
if eq get jfair 2 add k 1
rs = add ulong x 1
end
put jstat 5 add get jstat 5 1
else
e = jn_rec 5 get jjob add b 1 o 0
if ne e 0
ret e
end
put jstat 4 add get jstat 4 1
end
end
end
if ne get jfair 3 0
if ne sched_frestore get jfair 1 get jfair 0 rs 0
ret 31
end
end
sched_jattach true
ret 0
end

note Recovery: the outcome job entry k is released with (2 performed, 0
note UNKNOWN, 300 cancelled), or 999 when it is to be admitted again.
fn jn_rout k ulong to ulong
b = mul k 8
o = ulong 999
a = get jjob add b 7
if gt a 0
s = get jact add mul sub a 1 16 6
if eq s 4
o = 2
end
if eq s 3
o = 0
end
end
if and eq o 999 ne get jjob add b 6 0
o = 300
end
ret o
end

note Recovery: admit job entry k again into its recorded slot, ready again
note when a publication had made it ready, then its bypass count and goal.
note The slot, or < 0 when the scheduler refuses any of them (a recorded
note slot that is taken, a bypass count on a job that is not ready).
fn jn_readmit k ulong to long
b = mul k 8
x = sched_admits get jjob add b 1 get jjob add b 2 get jjob add b 3 get jreq k get jslot k
if lt x 0
ret x
end
j = ulong x
if ne get jrdy k 0
if lt sched_setready j 0
ret neg long 3
end
end
if ne get jbyp k 0
if lt sched_setbyp j get jbyp k 0
ret neg long 3
end
end
g = mul k 4
if ne get jgoal g 0
if lt sched_goal j get jgoal add g 1 get jgoal add g 2 get jgoal add g 3 0
ret neg long 3
end
end
ret x
end

note Admit job id durably: ADMIT, with the request and the slot it will
note take, is appended before sched_admits. -4 an id already in the journal
note (checked first, so a duplicate never takes or refreshes an admission
note ticket), -8 a request no capacity could ever hold, -2 when sched_room
note refuses (admission limit, no free slot, or ticket holders ahead), -5
note the journal refused, else the slot.
fn jn_admitr id ulong deps ulong flags ulong req ulong to long
if ge jn_jfind id 0
ret neg long 4
end
if not sched_feas req
ret neg long 8
end
if not sched_room id
ret neg long 2
end
s = sched_slot
if ge s 64
ret neg long 2
end
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 2
put r 3 id
put r 4 deps
put r 5 flags
put r 6 req
put r 7 s
if ne jn_append r 0
ret neg long 5
end
jn_hit 1
ret sched_admits id deps flags req s
end

note jn_admitr with no resource request.
fn jn_admit id ulong deps ulong flags ulong to long
ret jn_admitr id deps flags 0
end

note Creator: sched_policy, journaled first (POLICY, with the current
note capacities). -7 refused, -5 the journal refused, else 0.
fn jn_policy p ulong win ulong db ulong by ulong ttl ulong to long
if not sched_polok p win db by ttl
ret neg long 7
end
if ne jn_pol p win db by ttl sched_caps 0
ret neg long 5
end
ret sched_policy p win db by ttl
end

note Creator: sched_cap, journaled first (POLICY, with the current policy).
note -8 refused, -5 the journal refused, else 0.
fn jn_cap caps ulong to long
if not sched_capok caps
ret neg long 8
end
if ne jn_pol sched_stat 24 sched_stat 25 sched_stat 26 sched_stat 27 sched_stat 31 caps 0
ret neg long 5
end
ret sched_cap caps
end

fn jn_pol p ulong win ulong db ulong by ulong ttl ulong caps ulong to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 11
put r 3 p
put r 4 win
put r 5 db
put r 6 by
put r 7 ttl
put r 8 caps
ret jn_append r
end

note Creator: sched_goal for job slot j (waiting or ready), journaled first
note (GOAL). -3 no such job, -5 the journal refused, else 0.
fn jn_goal j ulong pro ulong est ulong unc ulong to long
if ge j 64
ret neg long 3
end
s = get sjst j
if or eq s 0 gt s 2
ret neg long 3
end
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 12
put r 3 get sjid j
put r 4 pro
put r 5 est
put r 6 unc
if ne jn_append r 0
ret neg long 5
end
ret sched_goal j pro est unc
end

note Release reviewed job slot j durably: RELEASE before sched_review. -5
note while its operation's DONE is not yet durable or on refusal.
fn jn_release j ulong to long
id = get sjid j
k = jn_jfind id
if ge k 0
a = get jjob add mul ulong k 8 7
if gt a 0
if eq get jact add mul sub a 1 16 6 2
ret neg long 5
end
end
end
if ne jn_rec 5 id get sjout j 0 0
ret neg long 5
end
jn_hit 5
ret sched_review j
end

fn jn_start op view ulong 4 cl ulong id ulong att ulong g ulong to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 3
for i ulong 4
put r add 3 i get op i
end
put r 7 cl
put r 8 id
put r 9 att
put r 10 g
ret jn_append r
end

fn jn_done op view ulong 4 o ulong id ulong how ulong to ulong
r = new ulong 16 0
put r 0 4
for i ulong 4
put r add 3 i get op i
end
put r 7 o
put r 8 id
put r 9 how
ret jn_append r
end

note Getters: whether job id is in the journal, released, its outcome; a
note recovery counter (0 torn bytes cut, 1 records read, 2 paused, 3 settled,
note 4 released at recovery, 5 admitted again); the fence; the generation.
fn jn_known id ulong to bool
ret ge jn_jfind id 0
end

fn jn_done_j id ulong to bool
k = jn_jfind id
if lt k 0
ret false
end
ret ne get jjob add mul ulong k 8 4 0
end

fn jn_jout id ulong to ulong
k = jn_jfind id
if lt k 0
ret 999
end
ret get jjob add mul ulong k 8 5
end

fn jn_stat i ulong to ulong
ret get jstat and i 7
end

fn jn_fence to ulong
ret get jfence 0
end

fn jn_gen to ulong
ret get jgen 0
end

note Action table entry k word i (k < 64, i < 16).
fn jn_act k ulong i ulong to ulong
ret get jact add mul and k 63 16 and i 15
end
